# Data layer

`ApiClient` owns the one `Dio` (host, timeouts, interceptors). It has no `/auth` or `/drawing` methods. Map `DioException` to `ApiException` before leaving this layer.

One client class and one instance per URL group, created in `app.dependencies.dart`. `/auth` and `/drawing` are examples — do not add empty clients.

```dart
// BAD — god client and a second Dio
class ApiClient {
  Future<void> login() { ... }
  Future<void> saveDrawing() { ... }
}

// GOOD — group client uses the shared ApiClient
class AuthApi {
  AuthApi(this._client);
  final ApiClient _client;
  static const prefix = '/auth';
  Future<AuthDto> login(LoginDto body) { ... } // POST /auth/login
}
```

- `AuthRepository` receives only `AuthApi`. `DrawingRepository` receives only `DrawingApi`.
- Repositories and ViewModels never import `dio`, `Response`, or `DioException`.
- DTOs stay in `data/api/<group>/`. Map to `data/models/` in the repository.
- Offline-first: read local first, then sync. `core/storage` is interfaces only; pick a DB later.
- Do not create a second `Dio` or a second HTTP package.
